{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498847-first-edition-nostalgia","id":1498847,"title":"First Edition nostalgia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-05T06:29:26-08:00","id":1498847,"title":"First Edition nostalgia","content":"Guys, have you ever been nostalgic about the first edition ? And if yes, why ?<br /> <br /> Before talking about the general *the second ed is hands down better*, let's start saying that forsaken first ed was already extremely cool in many ways.<br /> <br /> Is there something you still prefer from the first edition? Is there a chance you would like to play it again ?<br /> <br /> Personally I like both of them. Equally. First ed was my first newod/cod game and most likely my first favourite game from both line when I approached the wod/wod. <br /> Some of my players still prefer first ed.<br /> - more lethal , very lethal <br /> - you must prove the fact you are the best predator <br /> - hunt wise or die <br /> - less mechanical <br /> - general books vibe <br /> <br /> <br /> Please, just let me know what you like about it, or why you should play it again. I really dont wanna start an edition war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T07:39:20-08:00","id":1498854,"title":"","content":"I keep hearing that 1st ed was more lethal, I mean yes werewolves were weaker back then and gauru in 2nd ed is effectively a nuke but have you checked the part in the core about prey? Spirits in 2nd ed are still much more powerful than you, if you think that gauru alone will let you survive a one on one with a rank 4 spirit than you should reread it, hunting smart and planning accordingly is still paramount, granted, depending on the specific prey, you are less likely to die but not by that much, action economy is still a thing and being outnumbered by a bunch of rank 2 weaklings will still be huge problem and this is without accounting for when silver comes into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T15:19:24-08:00","id":1498894,"title":"","content":"Nope! Me and myplayers have basically never looked back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-05-2022, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T16:04:14-08:00","id":1498895,"title":"","content":"Never got to play Werewolf in First Edition. For Vampire; I think I preferred the the way the Covenants were written in First Edition. In 2E, some of them, specifically the Circle of the Crone and the Ordo Dracul, seem a little too much into &quot;being a better monster,&quot; or shedding Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T17:01:56-08:00","id":1498898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498847-first-edition-nostalgia?p=1498895#post1498895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never got to play Werewolf in First Edition. For Vampire; I think I preferred the the way the Covenants were written in First Edition. In 2E, some of them, specifically the Circle of the Crone and the Ordo Dracul, seem a little too much into &quot;being a better monster,&quot; or shedding Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition was...Not better at hiding it, but lamenting it openly, but all the Covenants are invested in being a better monster. They just have different ideas of what that means. Maintenance of humanity is an individual affair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T17:23:22-08:00","id":1498900,"title":"","content":"It's just I thought the one common ground the five Covenants had was a shared interest in maintaining the Masquerade, and an agreement that the best way to do that was by maintaining your humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T04:17:58-08:00","id":1498933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm nostalgic in the sense of it was when the IP owners were approving new books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the problem that the licensee isn't <i>pitching</i> enough new books that the owner can approve? For all I know OPP might pitch a whole bunch of books that's never been approved or mentioned to the fans, but my impression has rather been that OPP has a relatively low number of regular freelancers that already have close to maximum workload and won't pitch more books as a result.<br /> <br /> Either way, I definitely get why people would prefer the release pace of first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T19:04:58-08:00","id":1499010,"title":"","content":"My impression has been that, as freelancers need to eat and pay bills, that as the Paradox approvals have gotten more difficult to obtain, they've stopped bothering to pitch when they can pitch to Rich for Storypath books, or work for other companies, so they can keep their schedules as full as possible. The freelancers are going where the work is, and that's not CofD 2e as long as Paradox keeps up its current approval attitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T11:12:07-08:00","id":1499296,"title":"","content":"Yeah I love first edition. I absolutely loved the bleaker tone, that the wolves felt somehow more grounded. Everything had a more visceral vibe too. That\u2019s likely more down to writing style than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T23:16:41-08:00","id":1499501,"title":"","content":"I miss the big three not having colour art. That's partially me not being able to afford Premium books, but part of it is the monochromatic art in first edition and the other lines looking really nice. It gives this atmosphere that even the less vibrant colours of standard printing can't capture.<br /> <br /> As for the rules and setting, I only really got into CofD around second edition, so I'm having to remember the books I borrowed for a couple of weeks back in the day. Probably the fact that the idea of the hunt was intended to be more subtle, although I'm not sure how that would work out in play.<br /> <br /> But I'm also nostalgic(ish? I technically got into it after CofD) for the separation of Backgrounds and Merits in the oWoD. Even the most narrowly mechanically focused character was in theory forced to have some kind of tie to the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T07:27:30-08:00","id":1499518,"title":"","content":"The lore of 1st edition vs 2nd edition, lot of it is still valid don't get me wrong, but the new rules for hunting, the sacred hunt and its mechanics means that there is also a lot of revision needed to make it fit.<br /> <br /> There is also the gift lists when you compare the two versions, I'm tempted a lot of the time to just use the 1st edition versions if I could get away with it. I kind of feel shortchanged with 2nd edition gifts when comparing to the whole thing going for 1st edition, which is unfair, I know, just because of the number of books between the two of them.<br /> <br /> Kind of tempted to start a translation project to recover some of those gifts...if there isn't one already.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}